            <ArticleTitle>Acute autonomic neuropathy following primary herpes simplex infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>648-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 13-year-old girl presented with postural hypotension, severe abdominal pain and diarrhoea, parotid pain and a transient encephalopathy. There was evidence of an acute autonomic neuropathy and some electrophysiological evidence of a transient peripheral somatic neuropathy. The likely cause was primary herpes simplex infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
